    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n21433" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ilergavonenses</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Illurg-</span></b> ), ium, m., <i><span class="en">Liv. 22, 21,
		6</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Caes. B. C. 1, 60, 2</span></i>.—Called also
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ilergāŏnes</span></b> , um,
		m., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				people of</i> Hispania Tarraconensis, <i>on the
				sea-coast</i>, <i>near the mouth of the Ebro</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Plin.
				3, 3, 4, § 20</span></i>.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Illurgavonensis</span></b> ,
			e, adj., <i>of the
				Illurgavonenses</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cohors,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Caes.
					B. C. 1, 60, 4</span></i>
			.</div>
